WIRE.md §5.8: a map whose keys are known only at evaluation, here built by a comprehension over `["default", default]` of `ZzE | "default"`, holds two different keys that encode to the same text: E3317 at the second key (where its value was written); keys whose texts differ are fine. The keys print in their map-key text form (STDLIB.md §9.1: strings quoted), as check prints its static E3317.
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// E.
enum ZzE { default, other }

/// K.
type K = ZzE | "default"

/// Keys.
let keys: [K] = ["default", default]

/// Clash.
let clash: {K: Int} = { k: 1 for k in keys }

/// Other keys.
let others: [K] = ["default", other]

/// Fine.
let fine: {K: Int} = { k: 1 for k in others }
-- project.canon --
project demo {
  canon: "0.1"
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E3317]  a/a.canon:11:29
  clash: map keys "default" and default both encode to "default"

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
